868
01:00:13,230 --> 01:00:17,160
以下人员免除陪审义务
The following jurors are dismissed.

869
01:00:17,180 --> 01:00:20,730
陪审员 1号 3号 5号
Juror one, three, five,

870
01:00:20,760 --> 01:00:23,000
7号 8号
seven, eight,

871
01:00:23,020 --> 01:00:26,010
30号 32号
30, 32,

872
01:00:26,030 --> 01:00:29,100
39号 25号
39, 25,

873
01:00:29,120 --> 01:00:32,470
42号 43号
42, 43,

874
01:00:32,490 --> 01:00:35,180
49号 59号
49, 59.

875
01:00:35,210 --> 01:00:37,470
你们免除义务
You are dismissed.

876
01:00:37,510 --> 01:00:40,390
谢谢 你们可以离庭了
Thank you. You can go.

877
01:00:41,660 --> 01:00:44,370
富勒女士 通过刚才讲解
And do you think, Mrs. Fuller, based on that definition,

878
01:00:44,390 --> 01:00:47,720
您明白“排除合理怀疑”意思吗？
you understand the meaning of beyond a reasonable doubt?

879
01:00:44,390 --> 01:00:47,720
{\an9}【证据使陪审员对被告有罪的怀疑不再合理】

880
01:00:47,770 --> 01:00:48,600
明白
Yes.

881
01:00:48,630 --> 01:00:50,670
要达到不怀疑的标准
That to be convinced beyond a shadow of a doubt,

882
01:00:50,690 --> 01:00:53,500
在案发时非得亲眼见到吗？
you must have been there and seen the crime with your own eyes?

883
01:00:53,530 --> 01:00:54,990
不用 明白
Yes. I understand.

884
01:00:55,010 --> 01:00:56,360
大家都能以
And do the rest of you feel

885
01:00:56,380 --> 01:01:00,730
- “排除合理怀疑”作为评判依据吗？ - 是
- you can apply that idea, beyond a reasonable doubt, to this case? - Mhmm

886
01:01:00,750 --> 01:01:03,370
有多少人是父母？
How many of you have children?

887
01:01:03,640 --> 01:01:06,570
沃瓜德先生 有孩子？
Uh, Mr. Woguard. You have a child?

888
01:01:06,600 --> 01:01:09,380
嗯 是 索菲刚满四岁
Uh, yes. Soph just turned four.

889
01:01:09,400 --> 01:01:11,300
假设您女儿在公园
Say you and your daughter were at the park

890
01:01:11,320 --> 01:01:12,800
玩攀爬架
and she's playing on the monkey bars.

891
01:01:12,830 --> 01:01:14,720
您有几分钟没看她
And you turned your back for a few minutes,

892
01:01:14,750 --> 01:01:17,680
她跑过来说胳膊伤了
and then she runs over to you with a broken arm.

893
01:01:17,700 --> 01:01:19,090
您怎么判断？
What would you think happened?

894
01:01:19,110 --> 01:01:21,390
她从攀爬架上掉下来摔的
She fell off the monkey bars and broke her arm.

895
01:01:21,410 --> 01:01:24,770
对 这就是间接证据的例子
Yes, so that's an example of circumstantial evidence.

896
01:01:24,790 --> 01:01:28,590
根据事实可以做出的合理推断
That's what you can reasonably infer based on the facts that you have.

897
01:01:28,610 --> 01:01:30,660
沃瓜德先生 能明白吗
Does this make sense, Mr. Woguard?

898
01:01:30,680 --> 01:01:31,800
明白
Yes.

899
01:01:31,920 --> 01:01:34,510
要是有其他孩子跑来告诉您
And if instead another child ran over to you

900
01:01:34,540 --> 01:01:37,930
说看见她怎么摔的
and told you he saw her fall off the monkey bars,

901
01:01:37,970 --> 01:01:41,870
有人目击 这就是直接证词
that's direct testimony because someone witnessed it.

902
01:01:41,890 --> 01:01:44,290
大家能明白
Does everybody understand that difference,

903
01:01:44,310 --> 01:01:47,880
间接证据和直接证词的区别吗？
between circumstantial evidence and direct testimony?

904
01:01:47,910 --> 01:01:49,250
能
Mhmm.

905
01:01:49,270 --> 01:01:50,710
没有直接证词
Without direct testimony,

906
01:01:50,730 --> 01:01:54,600
就不能肯定犯罪一定发生
we cannot be positively certain a crime has been committed.

907
01:01:54,630 --> 01:01:56,050
作为检方
As the prosecution,

908
01:01:56,070 --> 01:01:59,710
我得把罪证明到排除合理怀疑
I must prove the defendant's guilt beyond a reasonable doubt.

909
01:01:59,740 --> 01:02:03,060
即 从现有的证据中
Meaning, that there is no other reasonable explanation

910
01:02:03,080 --> 01:02:05,470
不存在其他合理解释
that can come from evidence presented.

911
01:02:05,500 --> 01:02:08,020
谁是犯罪受害者
If any of you have been victims of a crime,

912
01:02:08,050 --> 01:02:09,900
请举手
please raise your hand.

913
01:02:10,710 --> 01:02:13,450
费伯先生 您遭遇了什么？
Uh, Mr. Faber, what was the crime?

914
01:02:13,480 --> 01:02:15,570
我被抢劫了 持枪的
Uh, I was robbed. At gunpoint.

915
01:02:15,590 --> 01:02:16,240
您认为
Do you have any reason to believe

916
01:02:16,270 --> 01:02:18,750
那次遭遇会妨碍您
that experience would make you unable to serve

917
01:02:18,780 --> 01:02:21,270
担任此庭公正陪审员吗？
as an impartial juror on this trial?

918
01:02:21,300 --> 01:02:22,470
不会
No.

919
01:02:24,070 --> 01:02:25,510
沃德小姐
Miss Ward.

920
01:02:26,660 --> 01:02:27,490
什么？
What?

921
01:02:27,520 --> 01:02:29,540
刚问到受害者时
When I asked who has been a victim of a crime,

922
01:02:29,570 --> 01:02:30,830
您举手了吧？
did you raise your hand?

923
01:02:30,850 --> 01:02:34,840
不是的 我不能讲这件事 就...
No, I realized I shouldn't share it. So...

924
01:02:34,860 --> 01:02:38,050
不能讲受害经历？
You're unable to share the crime?

925
01:02:40,230 --> 01:02:43,750
这样说吧 大庭广众说出来那事儿
It is frankly my worst nightmare to have to tell this whole room of strangers

926
01:02:43,780 --> 01:02:45,690
是我最害怕的
about the thing that happened to me.

927
01:02:45,720 --> 01:02:46,920
所以...
So...

928
01:02:46,950 --> 01:02:50,500
所以我才把手
that is the reasoning as to why I did not decide

929
01:02:50,530 --> 01:02:52,810
又放下来了
to continue having my hand raised.

930
01:02:52,830 --> 01:02:54,010
见谅
Thank you.

931
01:02:55,690 --> 01:02:58,690
那次遭遇会妨碍您
Do you think the crime would make you unable to serve

932
01:02:58,710 --> 01:03:01,200
担任此庭公正陪审员吗？
as an impartial juror on this case?

933
01:03:01,220 --> 01:03:05,580
问得好 我一直在想这个
That is a good question, and one I've been thinking about.

934
01:03:06,470 --> 01:03:08,750
想出结论了吗？
Have you come to any conclusions?

935
01:03:08,770 --> 01:03:12,790
我觉得 退出陪审团更合适
You know, I think I would be better not being on the jury

936
01:03:12,810 --> 01:03:15,970
做别的事情为社会做贡献
and instead would do better fulfilling a different civic role.

937
01:03:16,000 --> 01:03:19,210
什么别的事情？
And what kind of civic role do you have in mind?

938
01:03:19,230 --> 01:03:23,410
谢谢你问 我是个教授
So, thank you for asking. I am actually a professor,

939
01:03:24,030 --> 01:03:26,930
还没转正 期待早日实现
part-time, hopefully soon full-time,

940
01:03:26,950 --> 01:03:28,890
教书很重要
which, teaching is important work.

941
01:03:28,910 --> 01:03:31,120
教学是很有意义的
I think teaching is important.

942
01:03:31,150 --> 01:03:35,290
有人说教师是最合适的陪审员
Some would say that a teacher makes an ideal juror.

943
01:03:35,320 --> 01:03:37,570
才不是呢 不
Absolutely not, no.

944
01:03:37,590 --> 01:03:39,400
你的问卷表上写着...
On your questionnaire, you wrote...

945
01:03:39,420 --> 01:03:40,480
哦 别 别
Oh, no, no.

946
01:03:40,510 --> 01:03:43,380
我没想到会被当众念出来
I did not know that we would be reading those aloud, so.

947
01:03:43,410 --> 01:03:45,300
“你朋友怎样形容你”
"How would your friends describe you?"

948
01:03:45,330 --> 01:03:49,040
“聪明”被划掉了 改成了个“高”
"Smart." Crossed out, then the word "tall."

949
01:03:52,010 --> 01:03:56,420
要是那遭遇让你有偏见 就会免除你
If the crime you were a victim of makes you biased, we will dismiss you.

950
01:03:58,230 --> 01:03:59,800
说了不会惹上事吧？
Can I get in trouble for telling you?

951
01:03:59,820 --> 01:04:02,150
你是受害者 怎会有事？
Why would you get in trouble if you were the victim?

952
01:04:02,180 --> 01:04:03,470
我不知道
I don't know.

953
01:04:03,490 --> 01:04:06,650
法律有很多不讲理的地方
The law makes no sense in my opinion.

954
01:04:11,490 --> 01:04:12,490
那...
I...

955
01:04:15,920 --> 01:04:19,130
那事我从未公开说过
I haven't said it out loud actually before.

956
01:04:19,160 --> 01:04:20,700
没关系的
Well, that's okay.

957
01:04:20,900 --> 01:04:22,520
你报警了吗？
Did you go to the police?

958
01:04:23,470 --> 01:04:24,560
没有
No.

959
01:04:24,760 --> 01:04:27,330
物证只有个扣子
All I had was a button,

960
01:04:27,360 --> 01:04:30,140
我也不想见他坐牢
and I don't want him to go to jail.

961
01:04:30,470 --> 01:04:31,930
为什么？
Why is that?

962
01:04:34,020 --> 01:04:36,140
他有个孩子
He has a kid.

963
01:04:41,600 --> 01:04:45,390
我希望给他个机会改过
I want him to stop being someone who does that.

964
01:04:46,200 --> 01:04:47,530
要是进了监狱
And if he went to jail,

